course: dictionary
lesson: 16043
title: Vicinity: near, or about
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Vicinity is a formal word. It means the area near or around a place. «Police asked people to look in the vicinity of the school.» The school is the place, and the vicinity is the streets and fields close to it.
explain: You can check your meaning by swapping it in. «Police asked people to look near the school» still makes sense, so vicinity means something like near or around. In everyday talk people say near or around, but you will often see vicinity in news reports, police messages and exams.
explain: In maths and number talk, «in the vicinity of» works differently. «The crowd was in the vicinity of 500» means about 500, roughly that number, not exactly 500. Look for the clue: the number is close to the target, not the exact answer.
fact: Vicinity means the area near or around a place.
fact: «In the vicinity of» a number means about or roughly that number.
fact: Vicinity is a formal word, so it is common in news, reports and exam questions.
fact: «The police searched the vicinity of the park.» means they looked in the area close to the park.
fact: Everyday words for vicinity are near and around, so swap them in to check your meaning.
exercise: «The police searched the vicinity of the park.» What does vicinity mean? | The gate at the far end of the park | *The area near or around the park | A playground with swings | The lake in the middle of the park
exercise: «The crowd was in the vicinity of 500 people.» What does this mean? | Exactly 5 people | *About 500 people | No people at all | Over 5,000 people
exercise: «There is a cafe in the vicinity of the station.» Which everyday word could replace vicinity here? | Inside | *Near | Far from | Under
test: «Please stay in the vicinity of the bus stop until your mum arrives.» What does vicinity mean here? | *The area near the bus stop | The bus itself | The timetable board | A bus driver
test: «The bill came to somewhere in the vicinity of twenty pounds.» What does this mean? | Less than one pound | Exactly twenty pounds | *About twenty pounds | Ten thousand pounds
exam: «Witnesses said the van was last seen in the vicinity of the old mill.» Which word means nearly the same as vicinity? | Far from | Inside | *Area around | Under
